"rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-4.0","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"Dataset S1 of the Bio-protocol article \"Filter-Aware Analysis of 40 Hz Auditory Steady-State Phase Locking in Band-Pass-Filtered EEG Exports\". One rat (B98), epidural frontal EEG, 40 Hz click train (40 clicks per sweep, first click at 1.000 s, last at 1.975 s). Sampling rate 1000 Hz; every sweep has 4000 samples (4 s). 50 sweeps were exported; 5 were manually rejected because of artifacts (sweeps 10, 22, 23, 25, and 37), leaving 45.\n\nFiles: (1) the export after the acquisition software's 38-42 Hz band-pass (2nd-order Butterworth design, i.e., band-pass order 4, applied forward from rest to each sweep), 45 and 50 sweeps; (2) the unfiltered export of the same sweeps, 45 and 50 sweeps; (3) the recorded stimulus channel, a copy of the square-wave click signal split off before the speakers (50 sweeps). The EEG exports are in microvolts; the stimulus channel unit was not stated. README.md describes the file formats; SHA256SUMS.txt lists the checksums.\n\nRecorded under protocol P240803, approved by the Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee of East Tennessee State University. The code that reads these files is deposited separately (see Related works).","descriptionType":"Abstract"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.24539621","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":1,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"api","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":1,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2026-11-25T17:42:45.000Z","registered":"2026-11-25T17:42:45.000Z","published":"2026","updated":"2026-11-25T18:14:04.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"cern.zenodo","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"cern